# Source Code

This directory contains the main Python source code for the
NASA FIRMS Active Fire Data Analysis project.

## Main File

`nasa_firms_analysis.ipynb`

This file contains the complete implementation used to analyze the
NASA FIRMS MODIS and VIIRS active-fire datasets.

## Main Components

The source code includes:

- Memory-efficient CSV data loading
- Explicit data type definitions
- Chunk-based data processing
- Single-pass aggregation
- Fire Radiative Power (FRP) statistical analysis
- Missing-value analysis
- Day and night fire-detection analysis
- Monthly fire-detection analysis
- Reservoir sampling
- Data visualization

## Sustainable Computational Approach

The program is designed to reduce unnecessary memory usage when
processing large datasets.

Instead of loading the complete datasets into memory, the CSV files
are processed in smaller chunks.

The project also uses optimized numerical data types and categorical
data types where appropriate.

## Code Organization

The Python code is organized using:

- Classes
- Methods
- Functions
- Type hints
- Docstrings
- Reusable plotting functions

The `FIRMSAnalyzer` class contains the main data-analysis methods,
while separate functions are used for data loading and visualization.

## Input Data

The program reads the following files from the `data/` directory:

- `small_dataset1.csv` — VIIRS J1
- `small_dataset2.csv` — MODIS
- `small_dataset3.csv` — VIIRS SNPP


